   recognize `show all`, `between … and …`, or `from … to …`. CSV ingestion also
   omitted `workbook_sheets` and `workbook_rows`, so the request used semantic
   top-K retrieval rather than deterministic row filtering.
2. When retrieval returned any source, `rag_service.answer_question()` called
   the LLM and unconditionally returned those sources with `grounded=true`.
   This also happened when the LLM returned the exact unavailable-information
   sentinel. The frontend then rendered every returned source without checking
   `grounded`.

The exact contradictory-response component was
`backend/app/services/rag_service.py`, `answer_question()` (the post-LLM return
path, currently near line 118). The wrong query route originated in
`backend/app/services/workbook_analysis.py`, `is_analytical_question()` (line
63), and `backend/app/services/ingestion_jobs.py`, `_extract_bundle_child()` /
