## Stale Follow-Up Context Fix - 2026-07-31 16:11:49 +05:30

### Investigation

- Live DB inspection of `backend/data/rag_new.db` found zero active
  `chat_contexts` records, so the latest grounded answer shown in the browser
  had not produced a saved server-side result plan.
- Candidate prior grounded turns considered for the failing `name them` request:
  none were present in `chat_contexts`; no timestamps, document IDs, or result
  plans existed for that active conversation.
- Because no valid context was available, the previous `resolve_follow_up()`
  condition returned `None` when `conversation_id` was missing. The request then
  fell through to normal structured workbook analysis, where `name them` was
  treated as an entity-list question and selected the Attendance workbook.
- Exact stale-context selection condition:
  `backend/app/services/chat_context.py` returned `None` for a reference-style
  follow-up when `conversation_id` was absent, allowing unrelated global
  workbook analysis to answer from an older/irrelevant Attendance source.
- Secondary risk found: latest context lookup ordered by `created_at DESC`.
  SQLite `CURRENT_TIMESTAMP` has second-level precision, so rapid grounded turns
  could tie and select an older row nondeterministically.

### Implementation

- `backend/app/services/chat_context.py:198`: latest context lookup now orders
  by autoincrement `id DESC`, ensuring the newest saved grounded turn wins
  within the same owner/org/conversation.
- `backend/app/services/chat_context.py:304`: reference-style follow-ups with
  no `conversation_id` now return the standard unavailable response instead of
  falling through to global retrieval or workbook analysis.
- `backend/app/services/chat_context.py:112-126`: source/result-plan mismatch is
  rejected at save time when structured row-plan document IDs are outside cited
  source document IDs.
- `backend/app/services/workbook_analysis.py:1177` and
  `backend/app/services/workbook_analysis.py:1224-1229`: stored structured
  plans now include typed `result_type`, display column, and bounded
  contributing values so totals/counts resolve follow-ups from their own result
  schema, not from generic people-list behavior.
- `backend/app/services/workbook_analysis.py:482-487`: multi-workbook automatic
  structured selection now requires minimum confidence, preventing weak numeric
  accidents such as unrelated column `A` from becoming a grounded total.

